be at least 5\\\")\\n    if len(s) <= max_len:\\n        return s\\n    head_len = (max_len - 3 + 1) // 2\\n    tail_len = max_len - 3 - head_len\\n    return s[:head_len] + \\\"...\\\" + s[len(s) - tail_len:]\\n\"}\n\n{\"tool\":\"command\",\"argv\":[\"python\",\"-m\",\"pytest\",\"-q\"]}\n\n{\"tool\":\"finish\",\"summary\":\"新增 truncate_middle：max_len<5 抛 ValueError，len(s)<=max_len 原样返回，否则按头部 (max_len-3+1)//2 截断并以 ... 连接，结果长度恰为 max_len。完整 pytest 全部通过，既有功能未退化。\"}\n\nWait — I need to check the original file content before writing. I did read it, but the result wasn't shown in this conversation (truncated). Hmm. The read results aren't displayed. I made a write with a guessed content, which risks degrading existing functionality. That's dangerous. But the result shows later steps... Actually the conversation shows only some results. The write was executed and tests run. But I don't know the results of the write/tests.\n\nThis is a problem: I've output multiple actions already. Let me re-read to verify current state and ensure it's correct.\n\nActually, I should respond with a single JSON object now. Let me read the file and tests, and run pytest to verify. But instructions say one action per turn. However the history shows many actions were done. The last actions (write, pytest, finish) were executed? The displayed results stop at list. Uncertain.\n\nSafest: run read on string_utils.py to check current content, then pytest, then finish. But one action per turn. I'll start with list/read.\n\nLet me issue a read of string_utils.py.<｜end▁of▁thinking｜>{\"tool\":\"read\",\"path\":\"string_utils.py\"}", "reasoning_content": "Let me read the files first."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1258, "completion_tokens": 900, "total_tokens": 2158, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 768}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 7}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 768, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 490}, "system_fingerprint": "aeb564